### Three things you should decide on

1. **08-16 video IDs are genuinely unrecoverable offline.** I tried matching digest text against cached transcript *content* — it produced only 4/23 confident matches with single IDs winning unrelated bullets at zero margin, so I **rejected it rather than fabricate mappings**. Those 23 entries carry a synthetic `unresolved-<hash>` id (required — `_build_video_lookup` silently drops falsy ids) plus a YouTube *search* URL, tagged `id_status:"unresolved"`. Similarly 08-23 lost its titles at digest time, so those 22 use a clipped Core Takeaway tagged `title_status:"derived-from-digest"`. Both gaps are machine-readable and refillable.

2. **The 2 reindexed 2026-07-31 orphans are probably junk.** They hold the *same 3 videos* as the already-indexed `kimi-k3-and-the-open-weight-explosion-lo`, and both have empty analysis — superseded intermediate builds. Your viewer now shows 2 empty near-duplicates. Say the word and I'll drop those 2 index entries; vault counts are unaffected either way.

3. **`prism:graph-navigator` is broken plugin-wide.** Every dispatch fails with *"would be spawned with zero tools — unrecognized [codebase-memory-mcp, (all 11 tools)]"*. Its `tools:` frontmatter isn't parseable. I switched surface to `codebase-analyzer`/`codebase-locator` per the Stuck Protocol, but this is worth a fix in the Prism plugin since it silently disables your primary structural-query agent.

Note on I4: `/api/videos` and a "Library" modal **already existed** — I reused `_build_video_lookup()` and left both untouched rather than building a duplicate, so dedup rules can't drift between the two endpoints.
